# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Without this file, a Windows checkout rewrites every text file with CRLF
# line endings. The content is identical to what is committed (LF), but git
# reports the entire tree as modified, which makes `git status` unreadable,
# fails the prettier check in .husky/pre-commit, and blocks `git rebase`
# (which refuses to start with a dirty working tree).
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` tells git: normalize text files to LF in the repository,
# and write LF into the working tree on every platform. This matches what is
# already committed, so it changes no file contents.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never transform.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tgz  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
